# Final Diagnosis
The multiply method correctly computes the product according to the complex multiplication formula. However, the equals method compares the raw bit pattern of the real and imaginary parts using Double.doubleToRawLongBits. This means that +0.0 and -0.0 are considered different, causing equality checks to fail even when mathematically the numbers should be equal. The failing test case likely produces +0.0 in real part while expected has -0.0 (or vice versa), leading to the failed assertion.

# Methods to fix
The code to fix should be in the equals method of Complex, adjusting how zero values are compared to consider +0.0 and -0.0 as equal. Optionally, checks could be added only on numeric equality ignoring sign of zero.
